[] at the momement I don't know which chunk actually goes where, could some
[] one tell me how I can tell which order these go in?  I have mailed back
[] to nethack30_operator@sundown.ebay.sun.com, several times now but they
[] appear to be swamped and have not gotten back to me.  Is there anyone
[] else who had this problem and solved it and can pass some hints along
[] to me?

if the duplicates are truly duplicates then you should be able to
discard the excess files.  i found the file names/labels to be very
indicative of the order in which they were cut.  removing the mail
headers/trailers (as it says in the unpacking notes) and simply
"cat"'ing the files into an appropriate destination did the trick
for me.  i believe the file sizes are documented in the notes as well
(i.e. 60k chunks and as many as it takes to comprise the binary archive).

have some mercy on the auto-mailer/operator.  this is an extremely
generous and valuable service that can be negated, perhaps inadvertantly,
by a few careless actions (i'm not flaming the original poster, okay).

